# ASN.1 time strings taken from real certificates, with the instant each one
# names as OpenSSL decodes it.
#
# Provenance, and why it matters: these are the notBefore and notAfter fields
# of the 150 certificates in Debian's ca-certificates bundle, read out with
# `openssl asn1parse` and paired with `openssl x509 -noout -dates`. The
# expected value on each line is OpenSSL's reading of that string, not this
# library's - a corpus generated from our own writer would agree with our own
# reader about a shared mistake, and the two-digit year is exactly the place
# to make one.
#
# Regenerate with tools/asn1/extract_ca_times.py.
#
# <ASN.1 string> <Unix seconds, UTC>
